{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And as for you, you shall keep My covenant.</b> What is the meaning of 'And as for you,' and why did He repeat and say 'you and your seed'? This is its explanation: that the essence of the command was for the sake of his seed, for they need this external circumcision in order that through it they may arrive at the inner circumcision and the purity of the heart. But as for you, who already possess a pure heart, you did not need circumcision on your own account, but only on account of the whole world, as has been said. But his seed after him need circumcision on their own account. Therefore He said 'And as for you' with a vav of continuation — that you too shall keep this external covenant. And He gave a second reason for the matter: that if you too keep My covenant, then your seed will learn from you and do likewise; this is what He said: 'you and your seed after you throughout their generations.' And He said, 'This is My covenant which you shall keep, between Me and you' (Genesis 17:10) — that is to say: for the generations, the purpose of circumcision is nothing but to bring them to the circumcision of the foreskin of the heart, a matter entrusted between Me and you alone. 'And it shall be a sign of the covenant between Me and you' (Genesis 17:11) — that this external circumcision is a visible sign of the inner covenant entrusted to the heart, which is between Me and you. 'And My covenant shall be in your flesh for an everlasting covenant' (Genesis 17:13) — that is to say: for a covenant that all who enter the world shall recognize in it. And the Holy One, blessed be He, repeated this matter several times, to indicate that the essential reason for this external circumcision is to arrive through it at the purity of the inner heart."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:23.472682560Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}